        "topic": "Permutations and Combinations",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2001",
        "question_text": "<p>In how many ways can 5 students be seated in a row if two particular students must sit next to each other?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Treat the two particular students as a single entity. This gives $4$ entities to arrange: $(AB), C, D, E$.<br><br>The number of ways to arrange these $4$ entities is $4! = 24$.<br><br>The two students can switch places within their entity in $2!$ ways.<br><br>Total arrangements: $4! \\times 2! = 24 \\times 2 = 48$.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
